# latest.json is a derived pointer: always a copy of the newest file in the same
# directory. Tracking it means every pair of concurrent runs conflicts on it, which
# happened the first day the scheduled rail and a manual run overlapped. Nothing reads
# it from git — probe, freshness, export and the watchdog all glob the run directory
# and exclude it by name — so it is written locally and not versioned.
runs/latest.json
runs-freshness/latest.json
runs-graph/latest.json
